 had once  been the streets of New York City every  inch of his body covered up with a  special anti-sung suit of his own making  in the early days the SCP Foundation had  Mass release tutorials on how to build  full coverage suits out of clothes and  everyday household objects this had  likely saved many lives or at least  served to extend them for a while  sometimes that was the best you could  hope for David knew where he was going a  nearby underground parking complex  completely covered up beneath the Earth  where no natural light would reach the  people down there had constructed their  own generators to have working  electricity from emergencies and blocked  off any stairs or roadways to another  level the only way up or down was a  single Elevator Shaft that they owned  and operated it was the best way to keep  one of those Blobby monsters from  descending and dragging them all up to  the horrors of daylight David found the  place definitely avoiding any of the  monsters still roaming the streets he'd  been out on a food run collecting canned  goods from distant bodegas tuna spam hot  dogs soups they sent out four scavengers  a day in hopes of keeping Their Food  Supplies well stocked drawing straws  each day to decide fairly today David  had been one of them and it had been a  good day insofar as any day can be good  in this world on some days when they'd  sent out four scavengers only one two or  none at all had returned such is the way  with the world of the broken Sun you  quickly lost your sense of what's fair  if you wanted to survive here David had  learned that the hard way he reached the  elevator powered by the generators below  and knocked the secret code onto the  metal to get the doors to open He  Slipped inside and once the security  camera above saw it was him it descended  soon enough he was with the others  handing in the knights taking so they  could pool their resources and the most  experienced Cooks among them could  prepare tonight's dinner they took small  Pleasures in life whenever they could be  found later that same evening David and  four others Gus Addison Charlie and Mike  sat around a campfire eating cooked spam  out of their respective cans with  scavenged Forks they did all they could  to contact the world outside posting  messages online coded audio over any  working radio and ham frequencies even  leaving notes out in the open with Clues  to their location where the blobs whose  Minds were as melted and warped as their  bodies could never find them they  received correspondences from all over  the new world and with them came plenty  of interesting new stories to share so  that was precisely what they did around  the underground campfire every night  using filters they'd stolen from above  to keep the air pure they told each  other stories Gus had heard an  interesting one apparently out west  there was some kind of monster a  sculpture made out of concrete and rebar  that only moved when you weren't looking  at it this Beast stalked through the  dark seemingly indestructible and would  snap the necks of anyone and everyone it  managed to get its Rusty stretches of  rebar on in the world before this would  have seemed impossible but here and now  they were willing to believe it Charlie  told the story of a different Beast they  heard Tales of a group of people who  were holed up inside a mall in  Pittsburgh trying to wait out the  horrors nobody brought up the Dawn of  the Dead reference lurking in there but  apparently something else was lurking in  there too one day everyone who'd been  hiding in the mall was attacked and  slaughtered by some horrifying reptile  that tunneled out of the ground with  giant Claws and murdered almost all of  them in Cold Blood the one that escaped  had been telling his story to anyone who  listened nobody knew where the giant  reptile would turn up next Addison tried  to introduce a note of Hope with her  story she'd heard that out there there  was some mad genius working on a cure a  man who always wore a black cloak and a  white mask like one of those  old-fashioned plague doctors he'd come  closer than anybody else to synthesizing  a cure and he and all the others with  him were holed up in an SCP Foundation  site accepting help from anyone who  happened to wander by it would certainly  be a nice story if it were true but  nobody could really know for sure could  they Mike added a note of caution with  his story he'd heard of another group of  survivors who made their way to one of  those so-called SCP Foundation sites but  they'd found it abandoned devoid of the  many experts and saviors at the SCP  Foundation had promised in all of those  old broadcasts instead they were greeted  by a nightmare a ghoulish old man  covered in black slime with a permanent  sadistic grin on his face he could walk  through walls and melt off skin with his  burning touch he's always out there just  waiting for more unfortunate hope-filled  victims to fall into his clutches that  sent a shutter through them all what had  happened of course there was the obvious  problem of the treacherous burning Sun  up above and its melted minions down  below but how had the world suddenly  become so beset with these terrible  monsters it was like the Gates of Hell  had opened and all manner of beasts had  come spilling out all that the human  race could do now was survive but every  day the world seemed a little less worth  surviving for why were they here just to  be prey for these nightmare creatures  David who had been silent up to this  point finally spoke up asking have any  of you heard of the black Warrior there  was silence none have heard of this one  before they waited and listened he saved  my life David went on and I'd guess I'm  not the only one the incident as David  told it had happened weeks ago before  he'd even joined up with this current  group he'd lost everything and everyone  and was left wandering the wastes of New  York City alone he'd been hiding in the  dark of an old Financial building for so  long but his food supply had run  completely dry he would simply need to  leave he knew that if he waited any  longer even a few more hours without  food he'd pass out and dive starvation  in this sleep or be killed by one of  those things he'd need to go out in  daylight and forage it was the only way  he'd already built a total covered suit  what did he have to lose that very  thought would bring him closer to death  than he'd ever been before David  wandered out half Delirious with Hunger  trying to find a store that hadn't been  looted or burned down to nothingness his  vision was hazy he needed something to  eat and ideally something to drink too  he felt happier than he'd ever  remembered being when he came across an  abandoned Japanese grocery store and  filled up on stale rice and several  bottles of ramen like some congoing  teenager however while he may have just  saved his life in one way he'd put it in  grave danger in another the second he  stepped out of the store one of those  giant terrible flesh monsters saw him  his heart almost stopped as this  mountain of rancid liquefied meat  slithered towards him had shocking speed  sprouting a series of long tendrils  ready to grab him tear off his suit and  add him to its terrible Collective  trying to save his own life had  seemingly killed him of course David  tried to run but it was already too late  he felt the tendrils grab him and lift  him into the air pulling him towards the  immense and terrible flesh of this  rampaging super organism it called out  in so many warped voices at once crying  for terrible Unity David knew that in  Miram it would tear off his suit and  suddenly he'd be worse than dead but it  seemed that luck was about to shine on  him in the strangest of ways every  single one of the flesh monsters  gibbering voices became unified in the  blood curdling scream something swung  down and cleaved the mountain in 